WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
video file & English subtitles: Safex

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.002
After she lost Terry,

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:11.300
the only support Candy has
is Mr. Albert.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:19.641
At this time, Mr. Albert
got involved in a car accident.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:26.082
A thread of subtle recollections

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:35.494
Bad news!

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.731
Candy!

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.703
Candy!

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:51.549
She's not home?
What should I do? Candy?

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.381
Candy!

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.787
Candy!

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.223
What's up, Poope? You're so annoying!

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:11.934
Candy, bad news! Your brother...

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.766
My brother?

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.200
Is she talking about Mr. Albert?

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:21.276
Mr. Albert's out shopping.
He hasn't come back yet.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.309
I am coming!

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.210
What's the matter?

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.446
Candy!

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.280
What's wrong?

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:33.223
Your brother has been hit by a car!

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:39.557
He's in Happy Clinic right now.

00:01:39.707 --> 00:01:40.939
How's he?

00:01:41.089 --> 00:01:44.662
I'm not sure.
You'd better hurry up and check on him.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:55.441
Mr. Albert had a car accident.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.015
Why?
Why?

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.078
Parting with Terry...

00:02:00.228 --> 00:02:04.112
Stear left us.
Now it's Mr. Albert...

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.761
Here?

00:02:16.911 --> 00:02:19.630
Men, dogs, and cats
are all welcome.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.938
Why did they send him here?

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.575
Come on in!

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:33.011
Push harder! The door is broken.

00:02:33.161 --> 00:02:34.485
OK then...

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:40.785
Where's Mr. Albert?

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:43.286
Is that this patient's name?

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.727
Yes.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.730
He's taking a rest there.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.634
Mr. Albert...

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:02.715
He looks so lifeless!

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:09.214
Mr. Albert! Mr. Albert!
Open your eyes!

00:03:09.364 --> 00:03:10.782
What happened, Mr. Albert?

00:03:10.932 --> 00:03:13.724
Hey, slow down.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.518
Why didn't Mr. Albert answer me?

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:22.692
Calm down, have some coffee.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.167
No.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.071
I don't think
his injuries are that bad.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.876
Not that bad?
What do you mean?

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.281
That's right.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:45.619
Getting wounded is always
a serious thing. Aren't you a doctor?

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.952
Yes, I am.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.666
I can't say anything for now.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.968
You're such a lousy doctor!

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:02.732
How can a doctor examine
his patient this way?

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.341
Lousy doctor!

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:08.637
You are so energetic, Miss Negligee!

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:14.579
At least I'm wearing some clothes.

00:04:14.729 --> 00:04:16.884
I wear that because
I caught a bad cold.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.382
That's too bad.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:22.587
You're having a fever!

00:04:22.737 --> 00:04:26.894
I am all right. Mr. Albert
is more important than me.

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.225
I've already checked his condition.

00:04:30.375 --> 00:04:33.601
Before he regains his consciousness,
I can't give you specific answers.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.649
His head is injured.

00:04:36.799 --> 00:04:38.175
His head?

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.943
Mr. Albert has already
lost his memory.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.908
Now his head got injured as well.

00:04:44.058 --> 00:04:45.910
It's good.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.976
What do you mean?

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.747
He might regain his memory
because of this injury.

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:57.696
Do you think he'll get his memory back?

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:01.197
How could I explain that?

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:04.362
There's not much equipment here
in my clinic.

00:05:04.512 --> 00:05:06.392
I hope he won't get worse.

00:05:06.542 --> 00:05:10.868
Who sent him here?
Who did this?

00:05:11.018 --> 00:05:13.468
Calm down, girl.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.540
It was a passer-by.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:18.914
You are so energetic.
I guess the cold can't get you down.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:22.083
Have this medicine.

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:23.581
No!

00:05:23.731 --> 00:05:26.682
Ok, then we'll just wait
for him to wake up.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.691
Just take it easy.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.495
Let's play a game.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:41.596
This... That...No!

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.104
The Nine Circles?

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:47.435
Is he really a doctor?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.510
Put it inside here...

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:55.944
Open your eyes, Mr. Albert.

00:05:56.094 --> 00:06:00.515
You're not staying here.
I'm going to take you to the hospital.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:22.006
Isn't that me?

00:06:22.156 --> 00:06:25.812
Poope is on my shoulder.

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:31.387
A train? Where is it going?

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:39.427
Poope, where are you going?

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.958
Poope!

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:46.532
Alright.

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:49.905
Poope!

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.607
Poope!

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.772
Poope!

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:57.715
What happened?

00:07:05.158 --> 00:07:06.455
Mr. Albert!

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:09.819
Who's this girl?

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.155
This girl...

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.534
Candy...

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:21.897
Don't move.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.373
Lie down slowly.

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:31.115
Slow down.

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:35.449
He doesn't look like a lousy doctor.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.789
Where am I?

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:42.988
In Italy?

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:46.324
We are in Chicago, Mr. Albert.

00:07:46.474 --> 00:07:47.866
In Chicago?

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:52.796
Chicago? Right.

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:56.002
Candy, don't you have a fever?

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:03.184
Don't worry.
I'll take a look at him.

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:07.278
Head problems are very important.

00:08:07.428 --> 00:08:09.747
In the head, we have brains,

00:08:09.897 --> 00:08:12.950
nerves for sight and smell,

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:16.426
the pituitary gland,
proteins, amino acids,

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:20.655
fatty acids and collagen.
Its structure is very complicated

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.300
and it's indispensable.

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:28.502
I shouldn't judge him by his look!

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:31.035
How are you feeling?

00:08:31.185 --> 00:08:35.979
I believe your thoughts
are all messed up.

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:41.012
It will take a while,
your memory will gradually come back.

00:08:41.162 --> 00:08:42.452
Is that true?

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:47.081
The lousy doctor would not lie.

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:52.257
Sorry... I was so rude.

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:54.524
I believe in you, Doctor.

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:57.596
- Call me Martin.
- My name is Candy.

00:08:58.137 --> 00:09:01.470
And actually I am a nurse.

00:09:02.542 --> 00:09:05.102
The patients must be scared of you.

00:09:13.286 --> 00:09:15.646
Let him get some rest today
and come back tomorrow.

00:09:15.796 --> 00:09:17.416
Thank you.

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:29.093
That's great, Mr. Albert.

00:09:29.243 --> 00:09:33.764
You will soon remember
the first time we met.

00:09:34.206 --> 00:09:37.141
There were so many animals
around us.

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:41.741
After I remember everything,

00:09:42.214 --> 00:09:45.974
what will happen then?
I am so worried.

00:09:46.124 --> 00:09:48.109
Who am I?

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:51.084
What did I do for a living?

00:09:52.725 --> 00:09:55.592
If I recall my past...

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.096
Will it still be possible
to stay with Candy?

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:03.561
Are you feeling cold, Candy?

00:10:04.537 --> 00:10:06.368
Here, put this on.

00:10:07.907 --> 00:10:10.134
But what about you?

00:10:10.284 --> 00:10:12.268
You can't catch a cold right now.

00:10:17.216 --> 00:10:19.116
Thank you, Mr. Albert.

00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:27.685
That's warm.
Let's go home for dinner!

00:10:46.278 --> 00:10:47.643
Good morning!

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.838
Good morning, Candy.

00:10:50.616 --> 00:10:52.140
Are you going to work?

00:10:52.852 --> 00:10:54.211
Yes, goodbye!

00:10:54.361 --> 00:10:55.651
Goodbye.

00:10:56.622 --> 00:10:58.283
Take care!

00:11:03.729 --> 00:11:06.364
It must be really hard for her
to forget what happened with Terry.

00:11:07.066 --> 00:11:09.200
I believe Candy will be alright.

00:11:09.368 --> 00:11:12.303
We'll see her smile soon.

00:11:42.234 --> 00:11:43.531
Terry!

00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:52.337
Strasford troupe.
Romeo and Juliet.

00:11:53.112 --> 00:11:59.950
New Actor Terrius G. Grandchester
had a great success.

00:12:14.266 --> 00:12:16.632
Terry, congratulations!

00:12:17.336 --> 00:12:19.304
Thank you.

00:12:23.843 --> 00:12:25.469
What's the attitude!

00:12:25.619 --> 00:12:28.274
I can't forget it.

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:42.056
Madam, allow me
to give you a hand, please.

00:12:43.629 --> 00:12:45.790
- That's so kind of you!
- My pleasure.

00:12:49.068 --> 00:12:52.731
Stop!
I'm going to read you a story.

00:13:01.113 --> 00:13:03.104
Let's start.

00:13:12.925 --> 00:13:17.487
Did Mr. Albert
go to Dr. Martin?

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.598
I wish he could remember
everything as soon as possible.

00:13:21.901 --> 00:13:22.960
But...

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:27.836
Will Mr. Albert
start travelling once again?

00:13:29.175 --> 00:13:34.613
He'll take Poope
and his backpack and leave.

00:13:36.615 --> 00:13:39.641
After he recovers,
Mr. Albert will be definitely leaving.

00:13:41.921 --> 00:13:44.219
I will be alone again.

00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:46.614
Alone...

00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:50.655
I am not afraid of loneliness.

00:13:51.297 --> 00:13:53.561
I have lots of things to do.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:57.528
There's no time for me
to think too much.

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:03.964
Head nurse,
is there anything I can help with?

00:14:06.612 --> 00:14:10.007
Aren't you going to rest?
You've been busy since morning.

00:14:10.157 --> 00:14:13.978
No. I want to keep myself busy.

00:14:14.128 --> 00:14:17.982
Please take care of the patient
in Room No. 25.

00:14:18.132 --> 00:14:19.524
Ok.

00:14:20.259 --> 00:14:22.420
I am on my way.

00:14:26.332 --> 00:14:28.630
Dr. Leonard, this way.

00:14:29.235 --> 00:14:30.759
Thank you.

00:14:33.405 --> 00:14:36.670
Is Candice OK?

00:14:37.977 --> 00:14:40.377
She said she'd like to be busier.

00:14:46.652 --> 00:14:49.280
What will I do during lunch break?

00:14:50.256 --> 00:14:53.589
I would prefer some work instead.

00:14:57.396 --> 00:15:02.095
During wintertime, the trees
are waiting for spring to come.

00:15:03.469 --> 00:15:07.098
I am trying to recover
from the pain of parting from Terry.

00:15:08.607 --> 00:15:13.169
But, why can't I pull myself together?

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:16.640
No, I can't be brought down.

00:15:18.117 --> 00:15:20.415
But, who can't be brought down?

00:15:21.186 --> 00:15:23.586
How long have you been there for?

00:15:23.989 --> 00:15:27.718
Candy, you were so in your thoughts.
We called your name but got no response.

00:15:27.868 --> 00:15:29.787
I was daydreaming!

00:15:29.937 --> 00:15:33.662
You look so happy.
Are there any good news?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.901
We got a letter for you!

00:15:38.304 --> 00:15:40.272
Is it from Stear?

00:15:43.676 --> 00:15:47.305
He must have written it on the ship
going to France. His writing is wavering.

00:15:47.546 --> 00:15:50.014
Stear's writing is always like that.

00:15:52.084 --> 00:15:55.645
Dear Patty,
I am on the ship to France.

00:15:55.821 --> 00:15:58.462
It's really tiring on the ship.

00:15:58.612 --> 00:16:01.423
We have to clean up,
wash clothes, and also cook.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:06.160
Life in the army is totally
different from what I thought.

00:16:06.365 --> 00:16:09.459
Maybe it's the peace you're looking for.

00:16:09.768 --> 00:16:11.428
When you get this letter,

00:16:11.578 --> 00:16:14.734
I will be one of the
France Air Force.

00:16:16.041 --> 00:16:18.532
Stear, you...

00:16:19.078 --> 00:16:22.039
This is the letter for you.

00:16:22.189 --> 00:16:23.877
I'll read it!

00:16:26.085 --> 00:16:27.745
Welcome back, Candy.

00:16:27.895 --> 00:16:32.780
It must be very good that
Terry and you finally met again.

00:16:34.293 --> 00:16:36.727
Candy, this news...

00:16:40.399 --> 00:16:42.264
What's wrong, Candy?

00:16:43.736 --> 00:16:46.432
I can't hide it anymore.

00:16:46.772 --> 00:16:49.002
I broke up with Terry!

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:55.769
Terry is gone!

00:17:02.955 --> 00:17:04.923
Candy... Candy...

00:17:05.924 --> 00:17:08.825
Don't say anything, please...

00:17:09.595 --> 00:17:13.497
Don't talk about Terry again.

00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:17.824
So, you're doing this
because of Terry...

00:17:18.337 --> 00:17:20.870
Candy, I've thought...

00:17:22.608 --> 00:17:25.002
When you fainted on the train,

00:17:25.152 --> 00:17:29.844
you must have been so upset.

00:17:30.616 --> 00:17:33.547
But I had no idea.

00:17:34.353 --> 00:17:38.619
I didn't pay attention to you
because of Stear...

00:17:54.473 --> 00:17:55.997
I believe...

00:17:56.842 --> 00:18:01.575
it's enough that I had liked him.

00:18:01.847 --> 00:18:04.639
Besides, he's got Susanna with him.

00:18:04.789 --> 00:18:06.710
I should forget all the things
about him,

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:09.720
and stick to my dream
to be a good nurse.

00:18:10.255 --> 00:18:13.019
The lunch break is over, I have to go.

00:18:13.692 --> 00:18:17.154
Patty, don't forget to say hi for me
when you write back to Stear.

00:18:17.304 --> 00:18:18.526
Goodbye!

00:18:23.836 --> 00:18:26.771
Stear and Patty.
Annie and Archie.

00:18:27.272 --> 00:18:28.899
I hope that your relationships

00:18:29.049 --> 00:18:33.343
do not end up like
it happened to us.

00:18:42.421 --> 00:18:44.514
Candice.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.690
Come to my office.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.286
Yes.

00:18:50.529 --> 00:18:55.489
I want to send you
to the mobile hospital.

00:18:55.968 --> 00:18:57.299
The mobile hospital?

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:02.902
Yes. It's the hospital that will support
the railway construction workers.

00:19:03.609 --> 00:19:07.337
When the railway
construction moves to the inland,

00:19:07.487 --> 00:19:10.973
the hospital will be
moving along with the construction.

00:19:11.283 --> 00:19:12.944
When will this project be over?

00:19:13.218 --> 00:19:16.710
I'm not sure. I guess it'll
last until the railway project is finished.

00:19:16.922 --> 00:19:21.723
I hope you can complete
this mission.

00:19:22.461 --> 00:19:25.225
Is this fine with you?

00:19:33.872 --> 00:19:37.239
I hesitated becoming a nurse
in the army.

00:19:37.476 --> 00:19:41.173
But Franny said yes
without a second thought.

00:19:46.385 --> 00:19:48.615
If I accepted it at that time,

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:51.687
I would not have broken up
with Terry.

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:57.651
This place is full of sad memories.

00:19:58.163 --> 00:20:00.529
I'm going to leave them behind.

00:20:04.169 --> 00:20:06.330
I'll go, Dr. Leonard.

00:20:07.839 --> 00:20:09.602
You accept this job!

00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:15.870
Candy, don't worry about me.

00:20:16.481 --> 00:20:18.306
Dr. Martin will take good care of me.

00:20:18.456 --> 00:20:20.918
He's a nice guy.

00:20:21.553 --> 00:20:24.044
Candy, the problem is you.

00:20:24.423 --> 00:20:25.754
Me?

00:20:26.124 --> 00:20:27.949
You can't get over Terry.

00:20:28.099 --> 00:20:30.601
That's why you hesitate.

00:20:34.366 --> 00:20:36.391
If you're in this mood,

00:20:37.169 --> 00:20:38.795
then don't go.

00:20:38.945 --> 00:20:40.633
Mr. Albert?

00:20:41.306 --> 00:20:45.299
You can't take good care of
patients when you're absent-minded.

00:20:47.079 --> 00:20:49.013
Can you, Candy?

00:20:51.817 --> 00:20:54.877
Mr. Albert, I...

00:20:58.257 --> 00:21:01.818
Candy understands
Mr. Albert's words.

00:21:02.494 --> 00:21:05.327
To complete the mission of nursing,

00:21:06.031 --> 00:21:09.489
She made up her mind
dedicating herself to patients.

00:21:09.768 --> 00:21:11.258
I'll go.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:15.571
Candy makes this promise
in her heart.
